flowchart TB
    accTitle: Settlement authorization and error boundary
    accDescr: An authenticated settlement request checks role authority before selecting a trusted global, startup-scoped, or investor-scoped lookup, then evaluates payable state and maps safe errors through the shared RFC 9457 adapter.

    Caller["Authenticated caller"] --> Security["Spring Security"]
    Security --> Controller["Financial controller"]
    Controller --> Application["Financial application service"]

    Application --> Role{"Role allowed for operation?"}
    Role -->|"No"| Forbidden["FINANCIAL_OPERATION_<br/>NOT_ALLOWED · 403"]
    Role -->|"Yes"| Lookup["Trusted lookup selected by role: global, startup-scoped, or investor-scoped"]

    Lookup --> Found{"Settlement found in selected scope?"}
    Found -->|"No"| NotFound["SETTLEMENT_<br/>NOT_FOUND · 404"]
    Found -->|"Yes"| State{"Settlement initially payable?"}
    State -->|"No"| NotPayable["SETTLEMENT_<br/>NOT_PAYABLE · 409"]
    State -->|"Yes"| UseCase["Execute financial use case"]

    Forbidden --> Adapter["Shared RFC 9457 adapter"]
    NotFound --> Adapter
    NotPayable --> Adapter
    Adapter --> Problem["Allowlisted Problem Details"]

    Forbidden ~~~ NotFound ~~~ NotPayable ~~~ UseCase

    classDef error fill:#FEF2F2,stroke:#DC2626,color:#7F1D1D,stroke-width:2px
    classDef success fill:#ECFDF5,stroke:#059669,color:#064E3B,stroke-width:2px
    class Forbidden,NotFound,NotPayable,Problem error
    class UseCase success
